            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Life and Inspirations</strong><br>\nConstable's love for his native Suffolk, which he referred to as \"Constable Country,\" was a deep source of inspiration for his art. His personal life, including the loss of his wife, deeply affected his emotional state and, therefore, his work.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Exhibitions and Late Career</strong><br>\nTowards the end of his career, Constable organized several successful exhibitions in France and received more recognition. He continued to innovate, producing works with a focus on the mood and changing patterns of the countryside.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nJohn Constable died in 1837, but his vision transformed landscape painting. He left a lasting impression on the art world, with his works continuing to be admired for their truthful representation and emotional depth.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
